  "title": "The model shelf got crowded",
  "summary": "The model catalog grew in every direction while retries, monitoring, and new tools made that growth easier to use.\n\nNew text, image, and video choices arrived across two days: Qwen Image 3, Seedance 2.5, Muse Glimmer, Qwen3.8, Seedance 2.0 Mini and Fast, MiniMax H3, and Grok Imagine Image 2.0. Gemini, Muse Spark, Grok, and DeepSeek Pro also moved to newer versions. The existing Qwen Image and Seedance models were left alone.\n\nPrompt agents can now combine a system prompt, a Pollinations text model, and optional MCP tools, with editing through the dashboard or polli CLI and private or public My Models listings. A hosted MCP server adds nine tools spanning generation, embeddings, model discovery, status, and balance. Authenticated MCP requests also gained room to finish beyond the former automatic 30-second cutoff.\n\nFLUX, DreamShaper, and Z-Image gained ways to try another worker or provider after specified failures, with queue limits that keep requests from sitting behind a long backlog. For eligible non-streaming generation, an exact retry after a timeout can reconnect to work in progress or retrieve its cached result without another generation charge. Trellis 2 also moved to async provider jobs while preserving the synchronous Pollinations 3D response.\n\nModel Monitor now separates Official and Community health, excludes models without traffic in the selected window, and supports favorites and persistent filters. Community monitoring gained image-generation probes and a leaderboard for volume, median generation time, and success rate. Model discovery gained a community filter, while the catalog added shareable sorting and search.",
